C['deep']['extra'] = [_extra[2*i:2*i+2] for i in range(8)]
_np = [['Write one sentence naming the top three risks if the app fails, such as lost payments, locked accounts or wrong data, and spend about half your test time on those areas.', "Agree on 'done' before starting: for example, no open critical bugs, 95 percent of test cases passed, and every main flow checked on at least three devices."], ['Draw a simple map of screens as boxes and arrows, then count the paths from opening the app to finishing the main task; most apps have fewer than ten main paths.', 'Read the store description and any help page, then list five promises the app makes; each promise is a test you can write straight away.'], ["Write each test case with an ID, steps numbered 1 to 5, test data, and one exact expected result such as 'order confirmation shows total of 12.50'.", 'For every input field, test an empty value, the shortest allowed, the longest allowed, one over the limit, and a special character; that is five quick cases per field.'], ['Choose devices by sorting your users: pick one older low-memory phone, one recent mid-range phone and one tablet, and include both major operating systems if the app supports both.', 'On each device test with the screen turned sideways, with battery saver on, and after a phone call interrupts, since these three conditions expose many hidden faults.'], ['Write the title as a short sentence saying what happened and where, then list numbered steps, expected result, actual result, device, system version and app version.', 'Attach a screenshot or short screen recording under 30 seconds, and note how often it happens, such as 3 out of 3 tries, so developers know whether to chase it.'], ['Check speed by timing the launch from tap to first usable screen on a mid-range phone; under 3 seconds is a good target, and note anything over 5 seconds.', 'For safety, test that logging out clears the screen, that passwords are hidden, and that the app asks permission only for what it needs, such as not asking for contacts in a calculator.'], ['Group bugs by severity: crash or data loss is critical, a main task blocked is high, a wrong label is low. Count how many sit in each group to guide the release decision.', 'Look for clusters: if six of twenty bugs sit in the payment screen, recommend extra testing there rather than treating them as six unrelated issues.'], ['Write a one-page summary with tests run, passed, failed, bugs by severity and a clear recommendation: release, release with known issues, or hold.', 'After the fix, retest the exact steps from the original report and also run three nearby cases, since a fix in one place can quietly break another.']]
C['mods'] = [(m[0], m[1], list(m[2])+_np[i], m[3], m[4], m[5]) for i, m in enumerate(C['mods'])]
